# to[k] = from[k] between two arrays of doubles: the bytes are loaded and stored as they are, two elements at a time, whatever NaN they may spell.
# HOT-LABEL: steps by 16
# HOT: V128 b@[[first]] = Load(b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Reads:TypedArrayElements, {{*}}:GetTypedArrayElement)
# HOT: Store(b@[[first]], b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Writes:TypedArrayElements, {{*}}:PutTypedArrayElement)
# HOT-LABEL: end of loop
# Nothing compares the element with itself, looks at its bits or chooses another NaN.
# NONE-LABEL: steps by 16
# NONE-NOT: Equal(
# NONE-NOT: BitwiseCast
# NONE-NOT: Select(
# NONE-NOT: isLoopPoll
# NONE-LABEL: end of loop
# No turn leaves for an access by key, so the loop that takes one element at a time is five instructions, and eight of its turns are written out for the views that the wide loops do not take.
# X64: instructions: 19, patchpoints: 16, rare instructions: 28, {{*}} steps by 8
# X64: instructions: 4, patchpoints: 2, {{*}} steps by 2
